mainmenu "XEC I2C-NL target mode"

config APP_FAULT_SYNC_START
	bool "Time the injected bus fault from the START condition"
	help
	  Without this the delay to the pull is counted from arming the one shot
	  in the thread, and how long after that the transfer actually starts is
	  not fixed: a failed transfer is logged, the bus is recovered and the
	  port settle time is waited out. The delay has to be swept to find the
	  transfer at all.

	  With this the delay is counted from the START condition instead. A
	  GPIO interrupt on the SDA line of the target port, which pinctrl has
	  assigned to the I2C controller, reports the first falling edge of a
	  transfer, and the one shot is started from there. The delay then means
	  a known offset into the transaction, so a chosen byte and bit can be
	  aimed at rather than searched for.

	  Needs fault-sda-gpios in the zephyr,user node, naming the SDA pad of
	  the port the transfers use.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
